The iOS / iPadOS version of this product includes FFmpeg
(https://ffmpeg.org/), version 9.0.2: the libavcodec and libavutil libraries,
configured with only the MPEG-2 video decoder (mpeg2video) and the MPEG video
parser enabled. FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later. It is built without --enable-gpl and --enable-nonfree,
and it is linked dynamically as separate frameworks (avcodec.framework and
avutil.framework). The macOS version does not include FFmpeg.

  - Source code: the unmodified ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz is attached to each GitHub
    Release that includes the iOS / iPadOS version, next to the IPA. It is the
    same file as https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz
    (SHA-256 8c3850283eb25fa026482078a04051e0be17347b09ef81a0849bec15a96e002e)
  - How it is built: scripts/build-ffmpeg-ios.sh in this repository
  - The full text of the license (COPYING.LGPLv2.1 from the FFmpeg source code)
    is included in the app as FFmpeg-COPYING.LGPLv2.1.txt, and in this
    repository at Sources/iOSApp/Licenses/FFmpeg-COPYING.LGPLv2.1.txt.

